      "**Post-merge GitHub push self-heal is no longer aborting on legitimate merges.** `scripts/post-merge.sh` now adds a third accepted divergence class to the self-heal gate: if the remote SHA is an ancestor of HEAD (i.e. our local tree is strictly ahead — the textbook safe `force-with-lease` scenario), we push without scanning the file-level diff. The old gate only allowed `artifacts/mockup-sandbox/src/.generated/` and `attached_assets/` and was therefore failing on every merge that brought along non-trivial product changes, even though the underlying push was perfectly safe. The auto-generated allow-list is still consulted as the fallback for the genuine \"trees differ AND remote is a sibling, not an ancestor\" case.",
