    "content": "A large batch of new features and improvements across the entire dashboard.\n\n🗂️ MATCH DETAIL — GAME TIMELINE\nMatch detail pages now include a full game timeline graph (Net Worth, Experience, Level, Last Hits) sampled every 30 seconds throughout the match. Each player gets a colour-coded line — Radiant in greens, Dire in reds. Roshan kills appear as purple reference lines. Toggle between metrics using the tab buttons above the chart. Timeline data is captured from newly parsed replays only.\n\n🛒 ITEM PURCHASE TIMINGS\nBelow the timeline graph, a new Item Purchase Timings swim lane shows every significant item purchase for each player, with item icons positioned proportionally along the match duration. Hover any icon to see the item name and exact purchase time. Toggle it on/off with the 🛒 Items button. Consumables (TP, wards, smoke, dust, tango, etc.) are filtered out.\n\n🧙 SKILL BUILDS — REDESIGNED\nThe skill build display now shows ability icons per hero level (1–25) instead of raw numbers. Each cell shows the hero level, the ability icon fetched from Valve's CDN, and dot pips indicating how many skill points have gone into that ability. Talent choices are shown as purple T badges. Hover any cell to see the full ability name and the exact time it was levelled.\n\n🗺️ WARD HEATMAP PAGE\nA new Ward Heatmap page is accessible from the Tools menu. It displays observer and sentry ward placements on the Dota minimap, captured from parsed replays. Switch between all players (each with a unique colour) or filter to one player. Toggle between Observer only, Sentry only, or Both. Ward data accumulates with each newly parsed replay.\n\n🏆 ACHIEVEMENT BADGES EXPANDED\nPlayer profiles now display a richer set of achievement badges: Rampage, Ultra Kill, First Blood, Massacre, Ward Lord (100+ wards placed), and Ward Breaker (50+ wards destroyed).\n\n📊 MULTI-KILL LEADERBOARD\nNew /multikills page in the Tools menu — shows rampages, ultra kills, triple kills, and double kills across all recorded matches.",
