    "version": "6.64",
    "title": "Vanity profile slugs + admin Profile Spotlight",
    "published_at": "2026-05-09",
    "content": "**Task #208 — Pro-gated `/p/<slug>` short URLs and an admin-curated Featured Player rotation (full edition only).**\n\n**1. Vanity slugs.** New citext `vanity_slug` column on `player_profiles` (partial UNIQUE index on non-null rows so the existing rows aren't all colliding on NULL). Slug shape is locked to 3–24 lowercase a–z / 0–9 / hyphen, no leading/trailing hyphen, no `--`. The reserved-path deny-list (`api`, `admin`, `inhouse`, `tournaments`, `players`, `match`, `settings`, `pro`, `coaches`, `shop`, `leaderboard`, etc.) is enforced server-side so `/p/admin` can never be claimed. Server-side 302 from `/p/<slug>` → `/player/<account_id>` is registered BEFORE the SPA catch-all so the redirect works on first hit (no SPA boot required) and search engines / unfurlers see the canonical profile target. Pro membership is required to claim a slug; the picker also accepts read-only **grandfathering** for any non-Pro account that already owns one. New routes: `GET /api/vanity-slug/availability`, `GET/POST/DELETE /api/me/vanity-slug`. The picker lives in both **Settings → Profile** and the **Cosmetics Shop** (a new card linking back to settings). 30-day release cooldown is tracked in a separate `vanity_slug_releases` ledger; only the previous owner can re-claim within the cooldown — third parties get a 409 until it expires.\n\n**2. Profile Spotlight.** New `profile_spotlight` table (`account_id`, `headline`, `blurb`, `starts_at`, `ends_at`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `ended_at`). The bot's hourly cron (registered alongside the existing weekly recap / season-end / coaching crons in `src/discord/bot.js` `client.once('ready')`) calls the new `db.advanceSpotlight()` helper, which marks any active row whose `ends_at` has passed as ended. A new public `GET /api/spotlight/current` endpoint surfaces the most recently active spotlight (joined to `nicknames` / `player_stats` for the display name) and is cached 60s in-memory so the home page stays cheap under traffic. Superuser-gated `GET/POST/DELETE /api/admin/spotlight` powers a new `/admin/spotlight` page where operators can create new featured-player entries, schedule windows, and end them early. The home page renders a new `FeaturedPlayer` card under the Live Inhouse Pulse strip on both the signed-in and signed-out variants — hidden when no spotlight is active so the layout stays unchanged on quiet weeks.\n\n**Out of scope (deferred):** community edition (table only, no routes/page/cron), slug ownership transfer between accounts, algorithmic spotlight selection, per-spotlight images.\n\nFooter version bump v6.63 → v6.64.",
